Author: jingjiangze <1689170897@qq.com>
Date:   Sat Oct 10 23:26:10 2026 +0800

    perf: per-recipient bond strip in the compact public frame
    
    Step ③ of docs/ws-link-compression-next.md: a client that declares hello.pubBonds receives the hot m.public frame with players[].bonds only for the 1-2 players its screen can show (the field it watches or scouts, its own live field, else the remembered scope - the SETTLE result box keeps the unite/boss field's players after watchers was cleared), every other list travels as an explicit [] and is refreshed with one g.bonds -> m.bonds round trip (new optional C2S/S2C entries; the lobby refuses g.bonds without the capability and never sends m.bonds to a silent connection). The baseline, the shared compact frame and every frame for a client without the capability are byte-for-byte content-unchanged. Client: hello.pubBonds, actions.bonds on popup open, m.bonds written into the mirror player entry.

